#. Description of the plugin
#: verification-expiry-for-hivepress.php
msgid "Give a vendor's verified status an expiry date, per vendor or site-wide, so vendors must keep their profile up to date to stay verified."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:184
msgid "1 month"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:185
msgid "3 months"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:186
msgid "6 months"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:187
msgid "1 year"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the period chosen under HivePress, Settings, Verification Expiry, e.g. "3 months".
#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:413
#, php-format
msgid "Site default (%s)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:415
msgid "Site default (does not expire)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:421
#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:466
msgid "Does not expire"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:424
msgid "Verification Period"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:425
msgid "How long each verification lasts. The date below is filled in from this each time the vendor is verified, and again whenever this choice changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:433
msgid "Verified Until"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:434
msgid "The day after this date the verified status is removed and the vendor is emailed. Pick a date of your own, or leave it to be filled in from the period above. Blank means it does not expire."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:452
msgid "Verification Expiry"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:457
msgid "Verified Vendors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:458
msgid "A verified vendor keeps the badge until the date on their profile passes; then it is removed and they are emailed to bring their details up to date. These defaults apply to every vendor unless a different period is chosen on that vendor's own edit screen. Changing the default here does not move dates already set; select vendors on the Vendors screen and use the \"Apply verification period\" bulk action for that. Both emails can be reworded under HivePress, Emails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:463
msgid "Default Verification Period"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:464
msgid "How long a verification lasts unless the vendor's own edit screen says otherwise. \"Does not expire\" keeps the current HivePress behaviour, where a verified vendor stays verified until you untick the box."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:471
msgid "Reminder (days before expiry)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:472
msgid "Email the vendor this many days before their verified status ends, so they can update their details in time. Set 0 to send no reminder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:481
msgid "Expiry Email"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:482
msgid "Email the vendor when their verified status is removed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:483
msgid "The email asks them to check their profile, listings and contact details and to get in touch to be verified again. Untick to remove the badge silently."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:490
msgid "Verified Email"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:491
msgid "Email the vendor when they are marked as verified"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:492
msgid "Tells them the badge now shows and, when their verification has a date, when it is due for review. Not sent for the bulk action or when only the period changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:499
msgid "Badges to Expire"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:500
msgid "HivePress has two separate verified badges: one on the vendor profile, set by the Verified box on the vendor, and one on each listing, set by the Verified box on that listing. \"Vendor badge only\" leaves listing badges exactly as HivePress manages them. \"Vendor and listing badges\" makes every listing badge follow the vendor: verifying a vendor verifies all their listings, expiry or unticking removes all of them, and a new listing from a verified vendor is verified straight away. Choosing it also verifies the listings of every vendor who is verified right now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:503
msgid "Vendor badge only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:504
msgid "Vendor and listing badges, kept in sync"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:512
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:513
msgid "Your settings and every vendor's expiry date are kept if you delete this plugin, whatever the delete screen's generic warning says, unless you tick the box below. Deleting the plugin never removes anyone's verified status; it only stops the dates being checked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:518
msgid "Delete All Data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:519
msgid "Delete this plugin's settings and vendor expiry dates when the plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpve-verification.php:520
msgid "With this ticked, deleting the plugin also removes every setting on this page, the period and expiry date stored on each vendor, and your edited versions of its two emails, with no confirmation step and no undo. Vendors stay verified either way."
msgstr ""

